nostr-faucet (0.1.2-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The faucet is a nostr-ln consumer. Five modules deleted: grants,
    policy, rate_limit, state and control were a private rendering of a
    protocol that nostr-ln now renders once, and had diverged from the
    specification in five ways.
  * pay_onchain replaces pay_bip321. The faucet cannot conform to
    NWC-321, whose pay MUSTs support lightning or lno instructions, and
    should not want to: that method obliges URI parsing and pop/req-pop
    proof-of-payment handling on a server that holds RPC to a miner
    wallet.
  * NIP-44 replaces NIP-04 in the client.
  * CONFIG IS NOT COMPATIBLE. `owners` replaces `control_pubkey`, and the
    whole [policy] section is gone — per-key policy is kind-30198 grants
    published by an owner. Only [faucet.total_cap] remains, because it is
    a property of the faucet rather than of anyone asking. See
    /usr/share/doc/nostr-faucet/faucet.example.toml.
  * There is no pause, resume or status method. They were never in any
    specification. An open faucet is an OTHERS grant, and revoking it is
    what closing the faucet means — live, with no restart.

 -- DWDC <apt@dwdc.club>  Sat, 06 Sep 2026 20:15:00 +0200

nostr-faucet (0.1.1-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Probe fee funding at startup rather than failing the first request.
    Found by the 11.1 system test: a node without fallbackfee accepts
    requests and fails every one of them.

 -- DWDC <apt@dwdc.club>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0200

nostr-faucet (0.1.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Mission 11.1.
  * NWC pay_bip321, on-chain branch, backed by bitcoind.
  * Open policy: a per-key quota, a request rate limit, and a total cap
    that is refused even to a key inside its own quota.
  * Runs as its own user; the service dials out and listens on no port.

 -- DWDC <apt@dwdc.club>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0200
